-nail-art-the-money-trail-of-2026-assembly-elections/articleshow/134662872.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T22:09:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Arghya Prasun Roychowdhury</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134663102,imgsize-135646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav asks SP leaders to keep seat-sharing concerns internal amid friction with Congress]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadav-asks-sp-leaders-to-keep-seat-sharing-concerns-internal-amid-friction-with-congress/articleshow/134662978.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134662978.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav, president of the Samajwadi Party, encouraged leaders to express seat-sharing concerns privately. Tensions arose after Shiv Pal Singh Patel criticized Congress' demand for 150 seats in upcoming elections. Patel emphasized that Congress should receive a more realistic allocation based on their previous performance. Uttar Pradesh Congress president Aradhana Mishra stated that top leadership will decide the seat allocation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadav-asks-sp-leaders-to-keep-seat-sharing-concerns-internal-amid-friction-with-congress/articleshow/134662978.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadav-asks-sp-leaders-to-keep-seat-sharing-concerns-internal-amid-friction-with-congress/articleshow/134662978.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T22:07:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134663004,imgsize-46646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Example of their frustration': Shivraj Singh Chouhan slams Congress for